      "detailed_description": "<span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2431070/extras/903cc7fd66e446c19b12abf0db34a7d5.avif?t=1732908694\" width=64 height=64 /></span> <span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2431070/extras/396587d6d10c37cc972eca55a83cd18e.webp?t=1732908694\" width=128 height=48 /></span><br><br>The 98xx was an old computer OS from the 90s that’s recently been discovered after many years of being lost. There are still a few working files within the OS that can be explored, but there are a few unexpected glitches. One program in particular which goes by the name of &quot;Jumping Julian&quot; on the surface seems like your typical 2D platformer, but as the game goes on, weird things start to happen. Play at your own risk!<br><br>List of applications:<br><br>GAMES:<br>-Jumping Julian.exe<br>-Puzzle Patterns<br>-BallPopper<br>-Questions/Answers Game<br>-Talking Gerald.exe<br>-Tank Blast<br>-Asteroid Blast<br>-Matching Game<br>-Dancing with Darcy.exe<br>-Math Game<br>-Kingdom Quest<br>-Shape Game<br><br>SOFTWARE:<br>-Pixel Paint<br>-TypeWriter<br>-Photo Editor<br>-Video Editor<br><br>MISCELLANEOUS:<br>-Surfur (Web Browser)<br>-VidPlayer<br>-Documents<br>-Photo Gallery<br>-AudioPlayer<br>-DialCaller<br>-BookReader<br>-Settings<br>-Security<br><br>© Mirez Incorporated - 1998 <br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline crossorigin=\"anonymous\" poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2431070/extras/e9c8c7c5863b62a4be2bff92e441f6b2.poster.avif?t=1732908694\" width=128 height=128 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2431070/extras/e9c8c7c5863b62a4be2bff92e441f6b2.webm?t=1732908694\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"></video></span> <span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb